* Two-stage CMOS op-amp, open-loop AC and DC operating point (ngspice batch deck)
* Circuit: Settaluri et al., DATE 2020, Fig. 6 (AutoCkt two-stage op-amp, 45 nm BPTM).
* Adapted for as-data-sets from AutoCkt's netlist two_stage_opamp.cir (github.com/ksettaluri6/AutoCkt,
* no licence stated; element and source lines are AutoCkt's). Values written $$name are filled by
* string.Template (opamp_spice.py, or EMA's command_line interface).
.include "45nm_bulk.txt"

* sizing: all devices W = 0.5 um, L = 90 nm; m = parallel multiplier (real-valued here)
.param mp1=$mp1 mn1=$mn1 mp3=$mp3 mn3=$mn3 mn4=$mn4 mn5=$mn5
.param cc=${cc_pF}p
* held settings
.param ibias=${ibias_uA}u cload=${cload_pF}p vcm=$vcm vsupply=$vdd

* first stage: PMOS mirror load (mp1, mp2), NMOS input pair (mn1, mn2), tail mn3
mp1 net4 net4 VDD VDD pmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mp1}
mp2 net5 net4 VDD VDD pmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mp1}
mn1 net4 net2 net3 net3 nmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mn1}
mn2 net5 net1 net3 net3 nmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mn1}
mn3 net3 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mn3}
* bias: diode-connected mn4 fed by the reference current ibias
mn4 net7 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mn4}
* second stage: PMOS common source mp3, NMOS current-source load mn5
mp3 net6 net5 VDD VDD pmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mp3}
mn5 net6 net7 VSS VSS nmos w=0.5u l=90n m={mn5}
* Miller compensation (no nulling resistor) and load
cc net5 net6 {cc}
CL net6 0 {cload}
ibias VDD net7 {ibias}

* differential input around the common-mode level
vin in 0 dc=0 ac=1.0
ein1 net1 cm in 0 0.5
ein2 net2 cm in 0 -0.5
vcm cm 0 dc={vcm}
vdd VDD 0 dc={vsupply}
vss 0 VSS dc=0

.options reltol=$reltol
.ac dec $points_per_decade 1 10G

.control
run
set wr_vecnames
set wr_singlescale
set numdgt=15
wrdata ac.txt v(net6)
op
wrdata op.txt i(vdd)
.endc

.end
